{"id":"331dc2c5f12b223e26aa50fa594be0110d2a7ad43cc9319af84f0e87669938c4","lamport":1,"author":"scual.project@gmail.com","created_at":"2026-10-10T12:12:28.00655676Z","format_version":1,"kind":"set-field","payload":{"fields":{"description":"## What to build\n\nEach workflow becomes one lib call with one set of guards: Claim assigns and moves to assigned atomically; Promote closes the Writeup as CONTEXT.md says; reopening a ticket whose Parent is Closed is guarded; and \"unfinished Dependency\" has one definition shared by the lifecycle guard and the Next queue.\n\n## Why\n\nClaim is two separate writes done in both the CLI and the TUI, so the lifecycle guard can fail after the assignee is already written. The Writeup is closed by callers (CLI and TUI each do it), not by Promote. The invariant \"a Closed Parent has no open Sub-issues\" is enforced on create and re-parent but not on reopen, with no test. A missing Dependency target counts as satisfied in the lifecycle guard but as unresolved in the Next queue.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] Lib tests for: claim failing leaves no assignee change; promote closes and links the Writeup; reopening a child of a Closed Parent is refused (or the decision to allow it is recorded); dangling Dependency target behaves the same in close and in `ti next`\n- [ ] CLI and TUI claim and promote each call one lib function\n- [ ] One definition of unfinished Dependency in the lib\n- [ ] CONTEXT.md updated if the dangling-Dependency or reopen decision changes a glossary term\n- [ ] Existing CLI tests pass\n\n## Blocked by\n\nNone — can start immediately.\n\n## Notes\n\nBehaviour decisions (reopen under a Closed Parent, dangling Dependency) need the maintainer's call; implement the tests first and record the decision."}}}